{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789487805,"nonce":"XIQKT5u5eHKX0f4argH2NJjUBr8=","message":"First increment landed in 230867b, with ash 715cbdd and wren_lift f2e0826:\n\n- sched::reactor: a source is a handler the world runs on its main\n  context between turns; Signal::raise from any thread pushes a Ready\n  command through the endpoint, which wakes scheduler_idle; the handler\n  runs at the start of the next turn (schedule_step, after the drain\n  and the timers), with the world unborrowed and the handler out of its\n  slot, so it may add or remove sources. Raises during a run fold.\n- The world's source watch (World::watch_sources): a thread looks at\n  every loaded module's file (registry::sources, recorded by the Wren\n  loader) every 100 ms by mtime and length, queues the changed modules\n  and raises one source; the handler reloads them. Polling rather than\n  a notify dependency: the set is the loaded modules, tens of stats.\n- Every idle wait of the Haxe program is now the scheduler's: ash\n  715cbdd routes Sys.sleep and the frame loop's pacing through the\n  seam unconditionally, with ash's own sleep_ns keeping the old choice\n  (fibers alive -\u003e scheduler timer, else OS sleep told to the\n  collector). Lock waits on the main thread already went through park.\n- wren_lift f2e0826: a reload whose source fails to compile keeps the\n  module entry, so the next good edit reloads; before, the entry was\n  gone and the world saw \"not loaded\".\n- Test: crates/caribou-interop/tests/watch.rs (frame loop; a broken\n  edit then a good one from another thread; value 1 -\u003e 2; events\n  [(tune, error), (tune, ok)]).\n\nNot built: the socket poller (blocking socket reads still block the OS\nthread; needs an ash seam slot for I/O waits), the wasm host event\nsource in place of the nap, and events raised for TaskError/Log.","files":null}]}